cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this replication package, please cite the archived record."
title: "Replication package: What Does Agent Failure Prediction Actually Predict? Separating Task Difficulty from Run-Level Failure"
abstract: >-
  Code, analysis scripts, pre-registration and stored outputs for a study of what
  pooled AUROC measures in agent failure prediction. Decomposes pooled AUROC into
  within-unit and cross-unit components over repeated attempts of the same
  (model, task) unit, evaluates published and released monitors at
  online-computable prefixes, and compares task-level allocation against
  run-level aborting under fixed token budgets.
authors:
  - name: "Anonymous (double-blind review)"
type: software
